---
/**
 * /guides/bowman-2nd-job - Bowman 2nd job branches guide.
 *
 * Verification posture: Bowman's 1st-job kit CHANGED in CoT 2 (Power
 * Knockback moved from 2nd-job Hunter/Crossbowman kits down to 1st
 * job as a Bowman skill, replacing the removed Blessing of Amazon).
 * This directly affects 2nd-job kits - v83 Hunter and Crossbowman
 * both had Power Knockback. We're explicit about that shuffle below
 * and assume the rest of the 2nd-job kits are near-baseline pending
 * Founder's Access verification.
 */

import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Bowman 2nd Job Branches: Hunter or Crossbowman - Liven's Classic Maple Guide"
	description="Level 30 Bowmen pick between Hunter (bow) and Crossbowman (crossbow). Two branches, one weapon-speed decision. Full skill kits, build orders, and the Power Knockback shuffle that changes the 2nd-job kit composition in CoT 2 vs v83."
	currentPath="/guides"
	theme="henesys"
	decorations={false}
>
	<section class="section-heading">
		<div>
			<span class="eyebrow">2nd Job Branches</span>
			<h1>Bowman: Hunter or Crossbowman?</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				The Bowman branch decision is technically about weapon type
				(bow vs crossbow) but it's really about attack speed vs
				per-hit damage. Same six skills, mirrored across weapon
				lines. Here's the full kit, the build orders, and the
				Power Knockback shuffle that specifically affects 2nd-job
				Bowmen in CoT 2 vs v83.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<article class="prose">
		<div class="callout callout--framing">
			<strong>Verification (CoT 2 change):</strong> in v83, Power
			Knockback was a 2nd-job skill for BOTH Hunter and Crossbowman.
			In CoT 2 it moved <em>down</em> to 1st-job Bowman
			(<a href="/guides/skill-changes">datamine-confirmed</a>). So
			the 2nd-job kits below are v83 lists MINUS Power Knockback -
			you already have it by the time you branch. Whether Nexon
			added a REPLACEMENT skill in the 2nd-job slot is unverified
			until Founder's Access opens. The rest of the values remain
			v83-baseline.
		</div>

		<h2 id="summary">The two branches at a glance</h2>
		<div class="guide-summary-grid">
			<div class="guide-summary-card guide-summary-card--changed">
				<h3>Hunter <span class="status-pill status-pill--new">SPEED</span></h3>
				<p>
					<strong>Bow.</strong> Faster attack speed (Normal-5),
					lower per-hit damage. More Final Attack proc chances
					per fight. Smoother combat feel. Arrow Bomb (AoE
					stun explosion) is the star of the kit. Becomes
					Ranger at 70, Bowmaster at 120.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="guide-summary-card guide-summary-card--changed">
				<h3>Crossbowman <span class="status-pill status-pill--rework">CRITS</span></h3>
				<p>
					<strong>Crossbow.</strong> Slower attack speed (Slow-6),
					higher per-hit damage and higher crit multiplier
					ceiling. Iron Arrow pierces through mobs in a line -
					AoE via geometry instead of explosion. Becomes
					Sniper at 70, Marksman at 120.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2 id="the-decision">The decision, in one paragraph</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>Hunter for grinding, Crossbowman for bossing.</strong>
			Hunter's higher speed = more Final Attack triggers per
			minute + smoother DPS; Arrow Bomb's stun AoE dominates mob
			packs. Crossbowman's per-hit ceiling + Iron Arrow line-AoE
			is better vs single tough targets and dense corridors. Both
			branches feel great; pick the weapon aesthetic you like
			more, because at endgame Bowmasters and Marksmen are both
			top-tier.
		</p>

		<hr />

		<h2 id="hunter">Branch 1: Hunter</h2>
		<p class="section-lede">
			The bow branch. Faster attacks, AoE stun via Arrow Bomb.
			If you liked how Bowman 1st-job felt with the CoT 2
			addition of Power Knockback, Hunter doubles down on that
			control identity.
		</p>

		<h3>Hunter skill kit (v83 baseline minus Power Knockback, ~5 skills)</h3>
		<div class="skill-list-wrap">
			<table class="skill-list">
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th>Skill</th>
						<th>Type</th>
						<th>Max Lv</th>
						<th>What it does</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Bow Mastery</strong></td>
						<td>Passive</td>
						<td>20</td>
						<td>+Bow mastery %, +accuracy. Damage floor climbs closer to ceiling. Priority max.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Bow Booster</strong></td>
						<td>Buff</td>
						<td>20</td>
						<td>+2 attack speed for Bows. Consumes MP. Uptime maintenance.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Final Attack: Bow</strong></td>
						<td>Passive proc</td>
						<td>30</td>
						<td>Chance to trigger a bonus shot after basic attacks. Damage% scales with level. Bowman's biggest DPS multiplier.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Soul Arrow: Bow</strong></td>
						<td>Buff</td>
						<td>20</td>
						<td>Removes arrow consumption for a duration. Signature Bowman utility - eliminates ammo economy forever.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Arrow Bomb</strong></td>
						<td>Attack (AoE stun)</td>
						<td>30</td>
						<td>Single-target shot that EXPLODES on hit, dealing AoE damage + a stun proc chance to nearby mobs. Signature Hunter skill. Core grinding button.</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<p>
			<em>Note</em>: v83 also had Power Knockback in this slot at
			2nd job. In CoT 2 it's already yours from 1st job, so you're
			starting Hunter with one skill already "banked". If Nexon
			introduces a replacement 2nd-job skill in the vacated slot,
			we'll update this page after Founder's Access.
		</p>

		<h3>Hunter recommended build order</h3>
		<ol>
			<li><strong>Levels 30-35</strong>: 1 point in Bow Booster. Dump into Bow Mastery.</li>
			<li><strong>Levels 35-45</strong>: Max Bow Mastery (20 points). Max Bow Booster (20 for full uptime) or ~8-10 as filler.</li>
			<li><strong>Levels 45-55</strong>: Max Arrow Bomb (30 points). This is your grinding identity - the AoE stun is why you picked Hunter.</li>
			<li><strong>Levels 55-60</strong>: Max Soul Arrow: Bow (20 points). Frees you from ammo forever.</li>
			<li><strong>Levels 60-70</strong>: Max Final Attack: Bow (30 points). Late but the biggest DPS spike in the kit.</li>
		</ol>

		<hr />

		<h2 id="crossbowman">Branch 2: Crossbowman</h2>
		<p class="section-lede">
			The crossbow branch. Slower attacks, higher per-hit damage,
			line-piercing AoE via Iron Arrow. Better boss identity than
			Hunter but requires more patience with individual shots.
		</p>

		<h3>Crossbowman skill kit (v83 baseline minus Power Knockback, ~5 skills)</h3>
		<div class="skill-list-wrap">
			<table class="skill-list">
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th>Skill</th>
						<th>Type</th>
						<th>Max Lv</th>
						<th>What it does</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Crossbow Mastery</strong></td>
						<td>Passive</td>
						<td>20</td>
						<td>+Crossbow mastery %, +accuracy. Same math as Bow Mastery.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Crossbow Booster</strong></td>
						<td>Buff</td>
						<td>20</td>
						<td>+2 attack speed for Crossbows.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Final Attack: Crossbow</strong></td>
						<td>Passive proc</td>
						<td>30</td>
						<td>Same bonus-shot mechanic. Core DPS.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Soul Arrow: Crossbow</strong></td>
						<td>Buff</td>
						<td>20</td>
						<td>Removes arrow consumption for Crossbows.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Iron Arrow</strong></td>
						<td>Attack (piercing)</td>
						<td>30</td>
						<td>Shot that PIERCES through multiple mobs in a straight line. Signature Crossbowman skill. AoE via geometry - line up mobs, hit them all.</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>

		<h3>Crossbowman recommended build order</h3>
		<ol>
			<li><strong>Levels 30-35</strong>: 1 point in Crossbow Booster. Dump into Crossbow Mastery.</li>
			<li><strong>Levels 35-45</strong>: Max Crossbow Mastery (20 points). Max Booster (20 for full uptime) or ~8-10 filler.</li>
			<li><strong>Levels 45-55</strong>: Max Iron Arrow (30 points). Line-clearing on packed maps becomes trivial.</li>
			<li><strong>Levels 55-60</strong>: Max Soul Arrow: Crossbow (20 points).</li>
			<li><strong>Levels 60-70</strong>: Max Final Attack: Crossbow (30 points).</li>
		</ol>
		<p>
			<strong>Piercing tip</strong>: Iron Arrow's damage doesn't
			drop per pierce - each mob in the line takes full damage.
			Positioning is your DPS multiplier: fight in narrow
			corridors, line mobs up before firing.
		</p>

		<hr />

		<h2 id="progression">Common 2nd-job progression (30 to 70)</h2>

		<h3>Where to grind</h3>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Lv 30-40</strong>: Copper Drakes at Sleepywood.
				Fire Boars at Burning Land (for Hunter Arrow Bomb crowds).
				Ligators still viable at 30-35.</li>
			<li><strong>Lv 40-55</strong>: Wraiths at Kerning subway (Hunter
				Arrow Bomb crowd-stun heaven). Fire Boars stay great.
				Ludi PQ full window (35-51).</li>
			<li><strong>Lv 55-70</strong>: Death Teddies at Ludi. Coolie
				Zombies (Crossbowman Iron Arrow line-clearing). Ludi
				Maze PQ (55-70).</li>
		</ul>

		<h3>Gear buys at Lv 30</h3>
		<p>
			Hunter target: <strong>Ryden</strong> (Lv 35 Bow, cheap
			starter) or <strong>Bow of Magical Destruction</strong>
			(Lv 43, higher tier). Crossbowman target: <strong>Steel
			Crossbow</strong> (Lv 30) or <strong>Nisrock</strong>
			(Lv 43).
		</p>
		<p>
			Armor priority: DEX overall or top+bottom with 10% white
			DEX scrolls. Every point of DEX is bow accuracy AND damage
			(via mastery secondary scaling). LUK provides no benefit -
			ignore anything with LUK on it.
		</p>

		<h3>What to expect at 3rd job (70)</h3>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Hunter -&gt; Ranger</strong>: Strafe (4-hit
				single target shot burst), Mortal Blow (execute passive),
				Puppet (decoy summon that tanks mob aggro).</li>
			<li><strong>Crossbowman -&gt; Sniper</strong>: Strafe
				(4-hit variant), Mortal Blow, Puppet. Sniper's Strafe
				has higher per-hit but lower speed. Same skill
				philosophy, mirrored math.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 id="related">Related reading</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><a href="/jobs/bowman">Bowman 1st Job Guide</a></li>
			<li><a href="/guides/skill-changes">Skill Changes: v83 vs CoT 2</a> - Bowman is the class with the biggest 1st-job kit change</li>
			<li><a href="/guides/party-exp">Party EXP &amp; Grinding</a></li>
			<li><a href="/guides/exp-then-vs-now">EXP: Then vs Now</a></li>
		</ul>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
